{%- comment -%}
  WALLY DOMO: type loader for Horizon. Our file, not Horizon's.
  Rendered by one line in layout/theme.liquid and layout/password.liquid,
  right after Horizon's own font variables, so ours win.

  Adobe kit gag8aux (Marc's account; domains wallydomo.com, www, wallydomo.myshopify.com, localhost):
    arsenica-variable     100-800, roman + italic   (display)
    arsenica-text         400 / 700
    broadacre-regular-0   Typekit declares it at weight 300 (everything else)
    broadacre-medium-0    500 (very small type only, Marc's rule)
  Typekit names each static Broadacre cut as its own family:
  the CSS family is "broadacre-regular-0", never "broadacre".
  Quicksand 500 (Google) sits behind Broadacre so a kit outage never drops to Helvetica.

  What this changes: FONT FAMILIES ONLY, on Horizon's four roles.
  Sizes, weights, line heights, spacing and case stay Horizon's own settings
  (Theme settings > Typography). The font pickers there still show a Shopify
  font; what renders is the family below.
    body        -> Broadacre Regular 0
    subheading  -> Broadacre Medium 0 (small type only, Marc's rule)
    heading     -> Arsenica Variable (picker weight 300 = Dawn H2)
    accent      -> Arsenica Text (Dawn H1, card + print titles)
  Weight per role comes from the Shopify font picked in Typography (its weight
  variant, e.g. Inter Light = 300); the family itself is fixed here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://use.typekit.net" crossorigin>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://use.typekit.net/gag8aux.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Quicksand:wght@500&display=swap">
<style>
  :root {
    --wd-font-broadacre: 'broadacre-regular-0', 'Quicksand', system-ui, sans-serif;
    --wd-font-broadacre-small: 'broadacre-medium-0', 'broadacre-regular-0', 'Quicksand', system-ui, sans-serif;
    --wd-font-arsenica: 'arsenica-variable', 'arsenica-text', Georgia, serif;
    --wd-font-arsenica-text: 'arsenica-text', 'arsenica-variable', Georgia, serif;

    --font-body--family: var(--wd-font-broadacre);
    --font-subheading--family: var(--wd-font-broadacre-small);
    --font-heading--family: var(--wd-font-arsenica);
    --font-accent--family: var(--wd-font-arsenica-text);
  }
</style>
{% render 'wd-cta' %}
